Z||000000||Ed||11-04-2000||12:43 AM||||Anyone here taken any lessons from a driving school such as Russell's, Barber's, or Bondurant's?<P>I doubt that I drive anywhere near the limit of my car.  Do all these mod's discussed here help enough to offset road driving technique? <BR>This question does not include big engines for drag racing. <P>The classic example for me was an auto-cross where a participant couldn't use his own sick car (Pantera), but drove a RENTAL regular Thunderbird (non-SC, just a regular one) and lapped the same as everyone in their auto-cross prepared cars!  That showed me that technique is more than a little important. <P>Christmas is coming and maybe Santa will bring me a day at Russell's at Sears Point instead of some fancy tires or suspension.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Pontiaddict||11-04-2000||01:53 PM||||It's the other way around. Driving technique offsets all of the mods you have made.<P>If you're only pushing your car say, 70% and it's 20% better than stock. And someone is driving the car to 95% of it's ability stock. They should do better than you. (If my math is anywere near close.) <P>Of course, when you learn how to drive really well. The mods will be all the better.||||reg||1
